Z||000002||stimpy||11-11-2000||05:17 PM||||For a McLaren F1? Yes, no doubt that is a lot of money, but if you have the kind of "F*ck You" money it takes to buy one, I don't think you are out shopping for a bargain. Rember, the F1 i the no-holds-barred fastest street car in the world, and will no doubt remain so.  On top of that, buying a used one (being that they don't make them anymore) can pretty much guarantee an exclusive pedigree. Chances are the previous owner could be Mick Jagger or Mikka Hakkinen.<BR>Will they take my Fiero and a 94 Ford Tempo in trade on the downpayment?||||reg||1
